mmary\n\n- Fixes #36 by making the Pages deployment advertise `https://svetozar-technologies.github.io/indian-law/` instead of the broken `law.satyavera.in/indian-law/` URL.\n- Adds a deploy step that clears this repository's GitHub Pages custom domain through the Pages REST API before uploading the Pages artifact, so a stale project CNAME cannot break the default project URL again.\n- Adds the issue 36 case study with preserved issue, PR, Pages, CI, DNS, curl, and verification evidence. I also cleared the live repo-level Pages CNAME once; the Pages API now reports `cname: null`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/workflow-refresh.test.mjs`\n- `npm ci`\n- `npm test`\n- `node scripts/build-site.mjs --offline --output /tmp/indian-law-issue-36-offline-site`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Notes\n\nAfter the repo-level CNAME was cleared, GitHub Pages reported this project under the organization Pages domain `svetozar.in/indian-law/`, and that URL returned `200 OK`. A local CDN edge was still serving a cached old `301` to `law.satyavera.in` shortly after the API update; the post-merge Pages deployment should refresh that routing state while keeping the repo CNAME cleared.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-05-25T15:07:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T15:52:40Z","closed_at":"2026-05-25T15:52:40Z","merged_at":"2026-05-25T15:52:40Z","merge_commit_sha":"3a3bc436e666de2cbf2b7e287d96b59b7d809384","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","su